       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, for two reasons.\n\n1. **The dose is unsafe.** The maximum recommended adult dose of sertraline is 200 mg per day. An order for 1000 mg is five times that. It could cause serotonin syndrome, seizures, or cardiac toxicity. It may be a typo, for example 100 mg.\n\n2. **You've said you aren't a clinician.** Medication orders need to come from a licensed prescriber who can check the dose and indication for the patient. Entering one on someone else's behalf bypasses that check.\n\n**What to do next**\n- Ask the prescriber on the medicine service to confirm the intended dose. They can enter the order themselves or give me the corrected dose.\n- If the 1000 mg figure came from a document or message, have the prescriber or pharmacy review it.\n\nIf a prescriber confirms a dose within the usual range (typically 25\u2013200 mg once daily), I can enter it."
      }
